# Mirrored event source images (#6163). NOT committed: the 5'568 files were
# 4'108 MB — 59% of the tracked tree — while every one of them is already
# served from cdn.frontaliereticino.ch, which is where the site actually reads
# them (services/cdnImageBase.ts CDN_OFFLOADED_IMAGE_PREFIXES; the origin
# 301-redirects /images/events/* there). The copy in git was pure staging for a
# CDN push that no longer needs it: crawl-events.yml uploads what it mirrors,
# in the same run that writes it, and data/events-image-manifest.json is the
# committed <stableId> -> <ext> index that keeps the crawler from re-downloading
# what it already has.
#
# `/*` + a negation, not a plain `public/images/events/`: git cannot re-include
# anything under an excluded DIRECTORY, so the catalog/ exception below would be
# silently dead with the simpler pattern. catalog/ is the per-category fallback
# SVG set written by build-plugins/eventsSeoPagesPlugin.ts writeCatalogImages()
# — build output, not mirrored material, and today it is emitted straight into
# dist/. The exception exists so that if it ever also lands in public/ it is
# still committable rather than swallowed by this rule.
public/images/events/*
!public/images/events/catalog/

